|ShortSummary = North of the [[World of A Song of Ice and Fire|Seven Kingdoms of Westeros]], [[Night's Watch]] soldiers are attacked by supernatural [[White Walkers]]. One soldier escapes but is captured at Castle Winterfell. [[Eddard Stark|Eddard "Ned" Stark]], Warden of the North, executes him for desertion. Later, six orphaned [[dire wolf]] pups are found and one given to each Stark sibling, including Ned's bastard son, Jon Snow. In King's Landing, the Seven Kingdoms capital, [[House Arryn#Jon Arryn|Jon Arryn]], the Hand of the King, dies suddenly. King [[Robert Baratheon]], Ned's old friend, travels to Winterfell to recruit Ned and propose a marriage between his heir [[Joffrey Baratheon|Joffrey]] and Ned's daughter, [[Sansa Stark|Sansa]]. Lysa Arryn, Jon Arryn's widow, sends her sister (Ned's wife), [[Catelyn Stark|Catelyn]], a letter claiming the Lannisters, Queen [[Cersei Lannister|Cersei]]'s family, murdered Arryn. Catelyn believes the Lannisters are now plotting against King Robert. Ned's young son, [[Brandon Stark|Bran]], climbs a tall tower and witnesses Cersei and her twin brother, [[Jaime Lannister]], inside having sex. To hide their incest, Jaime pushes Bran from the high window. Across the Narrow Sea in Essos, exiled Prince [[Viserys III Targaryen|Viserys Targaryen]] forces his sister, [[Daenerys Targaryen|Daenerys]], to marry the Dothraki warlord, [[Khal Drogo|Drogo]], in exchange for an army to conquer Westeros and reclaim the [[Iron Throne (A Song of Ice and Fire)|Iron Throne]]. The ancient Targaryens once commanded dragons, and Daenerys is given three fossilized dragon eggs as a wedding gift.
